From f9b6a697e2032e289d2c29847c45fb9003c75ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 20:05:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: harden CPS descriptor configuration

Stage I1-I5 CPS descriptor updates before applying them, so failed
advanced-security validation cannot leave partially updated descriptor
state on the device. Parse staged descriptors into temporary packet
templates and commit them only after the full configuration validates.

Tighten CPS descriptor parsing by rejecting non-positive random field
lengths, checking packet size accumulation against MESSAGE_MAX_SIZE,
and cleaning up partially built packet state on errors.

Move CPS descriptor teardown until after handshake workqueues are
destroyed, avoiding races with queued handshake initiation work that may
still read descriptor state.
---
